# Run J (2026-11-07, user: "drop the 5km/h rule"): run I (pure SAC + PER, no noise
# pin, no cloning; slurm/il_finetune_c0_sac_per.env) with NO arrival speed
# condition. The limit in force was 10 km/h (v52_reward.env, raised from 5 on
# 2026-10-14); 0 = arrival on entering the 2 m goal radius at ANY speed, in the
# env reward (gated_reward._stopped_enough) and in HER's hindsight arrivals.
#
# Why: the critic-slope diagnosis found the warm-up critic crediting LOW THROTTLE
# for the +100 arrival -- the expert brakes over its last 10 m because arrival
# demanded <= 10 km/h, so braking and the bonus always came together (in reached
# episodes corr(throttle, return) -0.29, +0.21 once the last 30 steps are cut).
# Evals for this run: VAL_OVERLAY=slurm/il_eval_val_chw_jr_nb.env, VAL_TAG=jr35nb.
#
# THE PRELOAD WITHOUT THE ARRIVAL APPROACH (IL_PRELOAD_TRANSFORM=no_arrival): the
# recorded episodes that reached their goal lose their last 30 steps (the expert's
# braking approach -- built for the old speed rule -- and the +100) and end
# truncated. Offline diagnosis 2026-11-07 (scripts/offline_critic_slope.py, the
# fine-tune's own warm-up re-trained from c0): with the full preload the critic
# preferred steer -0.4 by +.051 and throttle -0.4 by +.096 / +0.4 by -.157 over the
# expert's action (as run I's live critic did); with this cut, steering is flat
# (+.003/-.004) and throttle flips to FASTER-is-better (-.037/+.046), which is what
# the reward pays. REDQ subset 10 vs 2 changed nothing. Online, arrivals (and HER's
# hindsight ones, now at any speed) still pay +100.
. "$REPO/slurm/il_finetune_c0_sac_per.env"
export GOAL_ARRIVAL_MAX_SPEED=0 IL_PRELOAD_TRANSFORM=no_arrival
